WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-ES

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.880
Hello.  Welcome back
to Lam Rim.

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:14.080
Today we're going to do a review
of the entire course.  It's

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.200
good for me.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.400
I'd like to do a review myself.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:22.320
This format of producing the episodes
separately

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:26.000
and then doing them at different times

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.080
seems to lose the flow of the entire
teaching.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:33.080
I thought it would be nice if today we went back to

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:36.120
the beginning and flowed

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:40.080
through all the teachings of Lam Rim
that we have had.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:42.800
I'm going to flow in that way based
on the idims,

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:45.080
the idea-images,

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:49.080
that we use to teach
ACI teachers.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:52.080
ACI teachers are expected to be

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:54.920
able to look at one
of these images

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:57.000
and identify the idea behind it.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:02.120
I think... Tim, how many did we say there would
be?  A thousand or something like that?

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:04.160
How many?

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:11.040
Something like 500.
So it's easy to take the test,

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:13.800
to examine someone based solely
on photos,

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:15.800
so we're only presenting you with
these photos.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:19.600
So I challenge you during this review:

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:22.920
when we put up a picture, I'll

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:28.040
give you a second and see if you can remember
what the picture was about.  Alright

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:30.160
?  This is a good review

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:35.080
of the entire course we are doing.
Okay, here we go.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:39.840
First image Mr. Sejii.

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:44.120
This image is supposed to
remind you

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:49.160
that we are halfway through the practices

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:51.400
for average-ability people,

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:55.160
and what they are trying to achieve is nirvana.  They are

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:57.000
trying to get off the Wheel
of Life,

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:01.720
out of all personal suffering.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:05.040
This is where Buddha taught
the three trainings

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:09.000
that will help you reach
your personal nirvana.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:14.120
The third training is understanding emptiness,
understanding the feather.

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:17.480
The second training is meditation.

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:21.480
At a deep level, these two
can only be done

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:25.080
in a quiet place, during certain
times of the day,

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:29.720
when you are really focusing
on your meditation mat.

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:35.640
At a deep level, these two should be done
during special times of the day,

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:37.840
but this one,

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:41.320
the basis of the other two, which is being kind
to people,

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:43.200
you can call it morality,

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:46.040
you could call it an ethical lifestyle,

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:50.720
but in the end it is being kind to people.

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:55.440
That is the foundation we always have
at our disposal all day long.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:59.880
This is one of the three extraordinary trainings
of Buddhism,

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:02.720
in order to help us achieve nirvana.

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:05.560
And we have it available all day.

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:07.600
So, in this image

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:11.840
you can see Seiji helping Geshe Michael
to decrypt his computer.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:17.560
Which is one of the nicest things young people
can do for older people.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:20.040
Next image.

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:24.520
See if you can remember
what this image was.  Did

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:28.880
you guess?

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:32.000
This lady is paying her taxes.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:35.520
What does this make it in the
Lam Rim system?  It

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:37.240
makes her...

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:40.480
a Dharma teacher.

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:43.600
When I say Dharma master,
or tantric master, I

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:46.040
already know the image you have in your mind:

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:50.680
it's a great lama on a throne
with a big yellow hat,

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:53.840
maybe they're ringing a bell

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:59.160
and a small drum and they're...

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:02.080
and you think, "'Oh, he's a Dharma master,
he's a real Dharma master.'"

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:06.280
Or you're thinking about that old picture
of Nagarjuna,

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:09.240
and it's all very mystical.

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:13.400
But in truth, in Lam Rim,
what we learned

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:17.320
was about this woman.

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:19.760
She has two children, is married,

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:22.120
and is a Dharma teacher.

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:24.080
She is a true Dharma master.

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:25.800
Pabongka Rinpoche said,

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:30.240
"Don't think that a Dharma master
has to be sitting on a throne

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:32.200
reciting some tantric ritual."

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:36.080
This lady is doing... what?  He

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:39.040
is paying his taxes.

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:45.160
Being honest with your taxes
is really difficult in my country.  It

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:48.240
can take weeks to prepare
your taxes,

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:50.680
to prepare them carefully,

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:53.000
to do them with complete honesty,

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:55.920
to pay every penny you're supposed to
pay.

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:58.080
This makes her...

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:02.680
She has the first of the
extraordinary trainings of a good person, to

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:04.320
be kind to people,

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:06.920
and that makes her a true
Dharma master.

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:09.280
Forget those images you have

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:11.280
of lamas with big hats,

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:16.160
and ringing bells.  That's easy,
anyone can do that.

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:19.040
Being kind to people is difficult,

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:23.600
and maintaining your morality, maintaining
your ethics, is also difficult.

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:26.320
The next one.  I'll

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:34.160
give you a moment.  Do you remember
what this is about?

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:37.520
The quote in the Lam Rim was:

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:40.640
(TSUL KHRIMS LDAN PA'I DGE SLONG
'OD DANG LDAN)

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:44.240
A person who is really keeping
his vows,

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:49.040
really keeping his Buddhist guidelines,
especially the ten rules,

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:51.640
shines, really shines.

00:05:51.640 --> 00:06:00.560
A person who is making a healthy,
modest, and discreet effort to keep their commitments,

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:03.480
to maintain the ten good karmas, to

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:05.720
be kind to people,

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:09.840
has a calm look on their face,

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:11.920
is glowing.

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:13.840
When they enter a room, you know it,

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:16.520
everyone starts to feel better.

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:19.120
Like Tim and Seiji.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:21.280
That is a light in the world.

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:26.400
Buddha said, "Those people are the light
of the world."

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:28.440
There is a Christian expression:

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:31.960
Don't put a candle in a basket.

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:35.120
Let the world see your happy face.

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:38.800
And that is a light,

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:42.400
a true guiding light for the whole
world.

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:46.480
Next image.  Idim number 4

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:56.280
Yes. This is a cliff I went to
with my partner Veronica

00:06:56.280 --> 00:07:00.400
for her birthday, during this Lam Rim.  They

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:05.000
were talking about the sunset,

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:08.880
whose word in Tibetan is (NUB PA).  It is

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:11.960
also the word for west,
because the sun sets in the west.

00:07:11.960 --> 00:07:15.320
So (NUB PA) means:
the sunset.

00:07:15.320 --> 00:07:18.320
And this is a very sad verb.

00:07:18.320 --> 00:07:22.840
This is a very sad idea in the Dharma.

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:27.080
The most famous place is at the end
of the Abhidharmakosha,

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:29.280
The Treasury House
of Higher Wisdom.

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:32.440
The Treasure House of Higher Knowledge,
of Master Vasubhandu,

00:07:32.440 --> 00:07:34.120
and he says:

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:40.480
"The sun of Dharma, the light of Dharma,
will be hidden in this world."

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:43.200
We will lose the light of the Dharma
in this world.

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:45.400
This world will enter into darkness.

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:47.720
After a certain time,

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:51.080
the Buddha's teachings will disappear
from this world.

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:56.080
First they disappear from
people's minds,

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:58.960
but they will still be in libraries; those books
are still in libraries.

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:01.840
Probably in libraries that John Brady has
not yet found.

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:08.200
And later they will also disappear from libraries,
and then they will disappear completely.

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:12.600
I put the photo here because Pabongka Rinpoche
made a special observation,

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:14.680
saying,

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:18.960
"If you cannot keep your commitments,
if you cannot maintain

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:21.400
'good behavior with people,

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:24.600
' then we can say that the Dharma
has left this world.

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:29.080
The light of the Dharma has left this world
within you."  "

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:32.200
The sun has set inside
your own chest."

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:36.080
Which would be a very sad thing,
if we don't keep our vows.

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:40.040
Next picture.

00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:50.920
Yes. We called this retreat Love
in the Time of the Virus.

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:57.160
The point was that during a
very difficult time in the world,

00:08:57.160 --> 00:08:59.080
if you keep your commitments,

00:08:59.080 --> 00:09:02.480
if you are kind to people

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:05.800
when things are scary,
frightening, the virus is spreading, we do

00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:08.240
n't know where, we don't know how, we do

00:09:08.240 --> 00:09:12.240
n't know how many people are going to
die...

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:15.920
If during those difficult times

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:18.240
you do something good for other people, it

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:20.920
is much, much more powerful.

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:24.840
He mentioned, if you remember, a 5-star Buddha paradise.

00:09:24.840 --> 00:09:27.920
Which is like a perfect place,

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:32.080
it's easy to be a good person, everyone
there is a good person.

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:34.080
That's not a great achievement. It's not

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:37.120
the big deal, and the seed
isn't that powerful,

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:40.200
being kind in a group
of nice people.

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:45.200
Being kind when people are attacking you,
when people are afraid,

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:50.040
when people aren't being kind to each
other, and being the one person

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:55.560
who stands up and shares things
in a difficult time,

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:59.720
then  That is an extremely pure person.
That is great karma.

00:09:59.720 --> 00:10:02.680
That is incredible karma,
much more powerful.

00:10:02.680 --> 00:10:06.120
I think the virus is a very good
time,

00:10:06.120 --> 00:10:10.720
a very good opportunity
for all of us to show: Are

00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:13.040
we truly Buddhists? Are

00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:16.400
we truly practicing the
bodhisattva path?

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:21.120
Can we help others even when things
are so difficult?

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:23.800
Next image.

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:32.480
This one is hard to remember; I have difficulty
recalling it. I'll

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:37.760
give you a second to try to think
about what this image is.

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:46.400
Okay. Pabongka Rinpoche was quoting
some books

00:10:46.400 --> 00:10:50.480
with a very, very common ending
from different books.

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:53.080
He quoted a famous one, which says:

00:10:53.080 --> 00:10:58.080
(BLO BZANG RGYAL BA'I BSTAN PA CIG)
(BLO BZANG RGYAL BA'I BSTAN PA CIG). It

00:10:58.080 --> 00:10:59.480
means:

00:10:59.480 --> 00:11:05.000
"May the teachings of the Victorious

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:07.560
Lobsang Drakpa, Je Tsongkhapa,

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:10.760
be spread throughout this world."

00:11:10.760 --> 00:11:14.840
And you're thinking,
"We have to go online,

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:18.800
we have to translate this Lam Rim
into many languages."  We must

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:24.280
try to spread the good word
to as many people as possible."

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:29.320
That's the end of the sentence, and we're supposed to
leave

00:11:29.320 --> 00:11:32.760
this Lam Rim class or video

00:11:32.760 --> 00:11:36.880
and share the Dharma
with people.

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:39.960
And we are supposed to spread the Dharma
throughout the world.

00:11:39.960 --> 00:11:46.080
And in this part of the Lam Rim,
Pabongka Rinpoche said, "Look,

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:48.600
the place where you're supposed to spread
the Dharma

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:52.200
is here, inside your own heart."

00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:55.960
Don't think that spreading
the Dharma means

00:11:55.960 --> 00:12:00.160
trying to translate the videos into more languages
or something like that.

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:02.960
That's a very important spreading
of the Dharma,

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:07.320
but he says, "If you spread it
in your own heart,

00:12:07.320 --> 00:12:09.560
then of course it will spread
out of you."

00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:11.760
Because the world comes from your heart.

00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:14.280
From your heart chakra, actually.

00:12:14.280 --> 00:12:19.080
Next picture, number 7.

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:23.640
Try to remember what
this picture was about. I'll

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:26.680
give you a second.

00:12:29.960 --> 00:12:34.280
Yes. This is one of my favorite themes,

00:12:34.280 --> 00:12:40.920
having a personal relationship
with another person,

00:12:41.800 --> 00:12:45.000
like the one these two people have.

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:49.440
In my opinion, and in Tantra, it's one of the
happiest things that can happen to you.

00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:54.120
It's one of the most wonderful things
that can happen to you.

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:59.840
Anyone can tell you that the reason
everyone is looking for a partner

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:03.480
is because it makes people happy; it's one
of the greatest blisses.

00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:05.920
When everything is going well,

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:08.680
it's one of the  the greatest joys you
can have.

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:15.040
But, you and I know that when it's not right, it's

00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:18.400
one of life's greatest miseries.

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:23.440
Why is this relevant to this course here?

00:13:25.680 --> 00:13:30.760
If your morals are good,

00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:33.440
it's the happiest thing in your life.

00:13:33.440 --> 00:13:35.680
And if you break your morals,

00:13:35.680 --> 00:13:38.040
it's the same thing that will make you miserable.

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:42.720
It's like having a good woman or man
as your partner;

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:48.920
the same person who makes you totally happy
can also make you totally miserable.

00:13:48.920 --> 00:13:51.760
So in this case, Vinaya,

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:55.960
your personal practice of kindness,
good behavior,

00:13:55.960 --> 00:14:01.920
is being compared to a partner
who can make the best thing in your life,

00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:05.080
or the worst thing in your life—the same person.

00:14:05.080 --> 00:14:09.400
Next idim. Number 8, I think.

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:17.080
This was a tricky one. Let's see
if you can remember it.

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:20.000
I'll take a sip of my green drink.

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:23.160
Thank you, Vinaya.

00:14:27.560 --> 00:14:29.560
Yes.

00:14:31.480 --> 00:14:35.440
This really represents breaking
your commitments.

00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:41.000
Pulling up a weed represents breaking
your commitments.

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:46.720
Why...? I mean, destroying this plant
is breaking your commitment.

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:53.960
If you're a gardener, you know you have to pull up
the weeds

00:14:53.960 --> 00:14:56.960
before the seeds are ready.

00:14:56.960 --> 00:15:01.400
If you wait until  So that the seeds are ready
to fall,

00:15:01.400 --> 00:15:03.600
and then you pull up the plant,

00:15:03.600 --> 00:15:07.120
you're going to scatter about a thousand seeds.

00:15:07.120 --> 00:15:10.120
By the next month or year,

00:15:10.120 --> 00:15:12.640
you're going to have thousands of weeds
growing again.

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:15.960
So you have to attack those weeds
in advance.

00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:23.400
This relates to a very radical statement
that the Buddha made,

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:28.920
(DGE SLONG DAG SROG DANG
BRAL ZHING SHI BA NI BLA'I)

00:15:29.680 --> 00:15:35.000
It is better to die than to break your vows.
Why?

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:37.160
When you break your vows,

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:40.600
you are setting in motion seeds

00:15:40.600 --> 00:15:45.040
that will continue to fall for
many lifetimes.

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:50.320
If you die, you ruin one
body-mind set.

00:15:50.320 --> 00:15:56.000
If you die, you ruin a very useful temple,

00:15:56.000 --> 00:16:00.080
a physical temple and a mind.
You lose one.

00:16:00.080 --> 00:16:02.840
But if you break your commitments,

00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:06.680
you lose many body-mind sets.

00:16:06.680 --> 00:16:09.800
You ruin your body and mind for many lifetimes.

00:16:09.800 --> 00:16:15.800
And you kind of set in motion the seeds
that are going to ruin many lifetimes. The

00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:18.320
Buddha was saying,

00:16:18.320 --> 00:16:20.960
"It is better to die than to break your vows."

00:16:20.960 --> 00:16:24.480
And he wasn't being metaphorical.

00:16:24.480 --> 00:16:30.080
He was speaking very literally
when he said that.

00:16:30.080 --> 00:16:34.320
Better to die than to break your commitments.

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:38.720
There's a joke in the Lam Rim.

00:16:39.520 --> 00:16:43.200
We take the  The vow not to renounce
bodhichitta,

00:16:43.200 --> 00:16:46.720
even at the cost of our lives.

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:50.240
There is a famous saying

00:16:50.240 --> 00:16:54.120
that throughout our lives we
are waiting to be

00:16:54.120 --> 00:16:58.640
thrown in jail by
some evil people.

00:16:58.640 --> 00:17:04.600
They come with a knife and say to you, "Renounce
your bodhisattva vows or die today."

00:17:04.600 --> 00:17:08.040
So we're going to say, "I choose to die."

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:11.120
And they kill us.

00:17:11.120 --> 00:17:15.680
I think we're all waiting... ever since
we took that vote, we've

00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:19.920
all been waiting for these guys to show up
with knives and threaten us.

00:17:19.920 --> 00:17:22.280
But in reality, we're the guys
with knives.

00:17:22.280 --> 00:17:26.080
We threaten our bodhisattva vows
every day.

00:17:26.080 --> 00:17:30.240
We have to make this decision every
day,

00:17:30.240 --> 00:17:35.120
when we carefully decide whether or not to keep
our vows.

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:39.560
It's hard to find those types who throw you
in jail and say,

00:17:39.560 --> 00:17:43.720
"I'm going to kill you if you don't renounce
your bodhisattva vows."

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:49.040
The following image

00:17:49.400 --> 00:17:51.640
is... See if you can remember it.  I'm

00:17:51.640 --> 00:17:56.920
going to give you a minute to try
to remember.

00:18:05.200 --> 00:18:07.920
This was a reference...

00:18:07.920 --> 00:18:11.200
we have the
"Mixed Nuts" translation team,

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:15.320
and we were translating an ancient
Vinaya text,

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:18.560
monk's vows, nun's vows.  They

00:18:18.560 --> 00:18:24.040
were talking about the vow, the tradition

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:27.280
that we shouldn't...

00:18:27.280 --> 00:18:31.240
when you become a monk or nun, they
give you your robes, they

00:18:31.240 --> 00:18:34.400
give you a small Buddha statue

00:18:34.400 --> 00:18:37.400
and they give you a strainer.

00:18:37.400 --> 00:18:42.000
And in ancient India, you were supposed to bring
this strainer with you.

00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:45.480
When you drink water from a stream, you are supposed to

00:18:45.480 --> 00:18:48.240
strain the water first

00:18:48.240 --> 00:18:52.920
to make sure you don't kill
any small insects.

00:18:52.920 --> 00:18:57.720
We mentioned a famous tradition
in the Vinaya,

00:18:57.720 --> 00:19:01.520
that if a couple of monks walk
towards the water,

00:19:01.520 --> 00:19:04.160
to a stream to get some water,

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:10.000
then they must choose the friendliest monk
to check the water.

00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:14.680
Don't choose the one who doesn't care
about insects.

00:19:14.680 --> 00:19:17.480
Try to find someone who loves
insects

00:19:17.480 --> 00:19:21.920
and ask them to check the water.  Because they will be
more careful.

00:19:21.920 --> 00:19:24.360
What's the point?

00:19:24.360 --> 00:19:28.520
We're talking about a type of ecological vows,

00:19:28.520 --> 00:19:32.120
where monks and nuns are
not even supposed to...

00:19:32.120 --> 00:19:34.080
pick green leaves from a plant,

00:19:34.080 --> 00:19:40.120
because they are the homes
of small creatures.  It

00:19:40.120 --> 00:19:44.640
means respecting even the
smallest votes,

00:19:44.640 --> 00:19:46.320
taking them very seriously

00:19:46.320 --> 00:19:51.320
because the results
multiply exponentially.

00:19:51.320 --> 00:19:58.000
So it's important to keep your morality
at a very subtle level, at a very fine level.

00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:02.080
And don't be picky.

00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:05.840
If I were to write the bodhisattva vows,
I would write an additional bodhisattva vow

00:20:05.840 --> 00:20:09.320
about not being fussy about your
bodhisattva vows.  There's

00:20:09.320 --> 00:20:13.840
nothing more irritating
than a person who...

00:20:13.840 --> 00:20:20.280
tells you they're keeping their vows and therefore
have to act like an idiot today.

00:20:21.080 --> 00:20:25.200
Keep your vows sweetly.  Keep them happy.  Do
n't exaggerate.

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:32.080
Don't bother people with your votes, because votes are
not meant to bother people.

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:35.720
Keep the votes small, keep them
quiet, keep them personal,

00:20:35.720 --> 00:20:37.920
don't advertise them.

00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:44.480
There is a saying in Islam: The left hand should not
know what the right hand is doing.

00:20:44.480 --> 00:20:48.920
It means, don't announce your votes.
Just keep them quiet.

00:20:48.920 --> 00:20:52.040
And keep them at a very fine level.

00:20:52.040 --> 00:20:55.440
Next image.

00:21:00.680 --> 00:21:06.480
This is the idea that being kind
to other people

00:21:06.480 --> 00:21:10.720
is like planting a tree.

00:21:10.720 --> 00:21:17.400
Oh, and today I went to the "Peach Tree Cafe"
to check something out, and

00:21:17.400 --> 00:21:22.040
Stanley, Allison, and I planted a peach tree there


00:21:22.040 --> 00:21:26.000
when we started the "PeachTree Cafe
Morning Show".

00:21:26.000 --> 00:21:30.440
And I want to tell you that this week there were
three peaches

00:21:30.440 --> 00:21:34.480
and... we already have peaches!

00:21:35.080 --> 00:21:42.840
What it means is: take care of the foundation
of your practices, take care of the root,

00:21:42.840 --> 00:21:48.000
plant good karma by keeping your vows and
being kind to people.

00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:50.560
Then that will grow into a tree.

00:21:50.560 --> 00:21:55.120
And that peach tree that we planted,
about five months ago, is

00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:58.680
already bearing a lot of fruit.

00:21:58.680 --> 00:22:04.120
If you didn't take care of him when he was little, you wouldn't
have anything.

00:22:04.120 --> 00:22:09.080
But if you take care of the foundation of your
Buddhist practice,

00:22:09.080 --> 00:22:11.440
which is being kind to people,

00:22:11.440 --> 00:22:14.280
then the fruits will be thousands
and thousands and thousands.

00:22:14.280 --> 00:22:18.680
It will come, and it will grow into a huge...
it will grow into a tree, it will bear

00:22:18.680 --> 00:22:24.000
peaches every year and for many years
you will have peaches.

00:22:24.000 --> 00:22:30.000
Keep, protect... this girl is
carefully protecting the outbreak.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:32.520
Protect your morality.

00:22:32.520 --> 00:22:35.320
Very good.  Next image.

00:22:36.240 --> 00:22:42.240
If I remember correctly, there were four conditions

00:22:42.240 --> 00:22:45.080
that could cause you to break
your commitments.

00:22:45.080 --> 00:22:48.000
If you took the Bodhisattva commitments

00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:51.120
or the Vinaya Pratimoksha commitments,

00:22:51.120 --> 00:22:56.120
or even if you took the Diamond Way commitments... tantric commitments.

00:22:56.120 --> 00:23:01.040
I think there were four of them.  Pabongka Rinpoche reviewed...
No, maybe more than that, anyway.

00:23:01.040 --> 00:23:04.960
There were certain conditions that would help you
break your vows.

00:23:04.960 --> 00:23:09.400
If you want to break your vows, there are some
special ways to do it.

00:23:09.400 --> 00:23:13.000
Here's the first one, which is:

00:23:13.000 --> 00:23:18.200
If you don't know what your votes are, then
that's a good way to break them.

00:23:18.200 --> 00:23:22.360
If you want to break them, then
don't study them.

00:23:22.360 --> 00:23:29.480
And one of my annoyances—I have many things
that bother me in the Dharma—

00:23:29.480 --> 00:23:33.440
is the teachers who give initiations,

00:23:33.440 --> 00:23:39.040
great initiations, and don't explain to the people
who are taking the initiation

00:23:39.040 --> 00:23:41.400
that they have just taken vows.

00:23:41.400 --> 00:23:45.800
There are hundreds of vows you take
when you have an initiation,

00:23:45.800 --> 00:23:48.840
and you're going to break them if you don't know them.

00:23:48.840 --> 00:23:52.160
It is the teacher's responsibility to

00:23:52.160 --> 00:23:56.840
train you on the vows before you
have an initiation.

00:23:56.840 --> 00:24:03.080
If they don't offer training, I wouldn't take
any initiation from them.

00:24:03.080 --> 00:24:07.600
The best way to break your vows, in the first place,
is not to know them.

00:24:07.600 --> 00:24:10.400
Read the recipe before you start cooking.

00:24:10.400 --> 00:24:14.160
That's what Veronica tells me every time I
cook.

00:24:14.160 --> 00:24:16.960
Next image.

00:24:17.000 --> 00:24:24.880
It's a lady saying, "Yes, it's not such a
big deal."

00:24:24.880 --> 00:24:29.840
That vow of, I don't know...

00:24:29.840 --> 00:24:34.800
not cutting green plants without saying a prayer,

00:24:34.800 --> 00:24:40.000
"Come on, that's a little extreme.
It's a little excessive.

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:45.960
That's not a big deal, it's just some insects
that might be using that leaf

00:24:45.960 --> 00:24:50.120
as a roof now and then,
so it's not a big deal."

00:24:50.120 --> 00:24:54.080
The second big way to break
your vows

00:24:54.080 --> 00:24:55.720
is to have this attitude:

00:24:55.720 --> 00:25:00.320
"Oh, that's not a big deal, I'm keeping
the bigger ones."

00:25:00.320 --> 00:25:03.560
Okay. Next up.

00:25:06.240 --> 00:25:12.840
If we have a klesha, meaning
if we have any kind of negativity

00:25:12.840 --> 00:25:17.400
circulating in our minds,
that's a great way to break your vows.

00:25:17.400 --> 00:25:20.080
Getting upset with someone,

00:25:20.080 --> 00:25:26.720
or obsessing over acquiring something, money,

00:25:26.720 --> 00:25:30.880
or clinging to our Netflix at night.

00:25:30.880 --> 00:25:38.960
That kind of... By the way, it's not wrong to watch Netflix,
but I'm talking about...

00:25:38.960 --> 00:25:43.080
hurting someone else because you want to get home
and watch Netflix. That's a problem.

00:25:43.080 --> 00:25:44.920
So,

00:25:44.920 --> 00:25:51.000
this is called "A Gang Fight,"
and the story is, what?

00:25:52.120 --> 00:25:57.080
Go after the big guy on the other side.

00:25:57.080 --> 00:25:59.600
Figure out who the leader on the other side is,

00:25:59.600 --> 00:26:04.720
and don't talk, don't negotiate, don't...  Scream,

00:26:04.720 --> 00:26:07.480
go up to him and hit him on the head.

00:26:07.480 --> 00:26:10.880
And then that whole side is going to fall apart.

00:26:10.880 --> 00:26:15.320
Identify your worst bad habit,

00:26:15.320 --> 00:26:21.160
and go after it first. That's the way
to keep your vows.

00:26:21.160 --> 00:26:24.040
The next one.

00:26:25.000 --> 00:26:27.800
If you...

00:26:27.800 --> 00:26:33.840
By the way, at the age of... my age, I'm not telling you
how old I am,

00:26:33.840 --> 00:26:37.080
but this whole young love thing

00:26:37.080 --> 00:26:42.320
is so ridiculous from my age's point of view
.

00:26:42.320 --> 00:26:46.400
And I can say that from experience because I've been through it
.

00:26:46.400 --> 00:26:48.240
But this thing of:

00:26:48.240 --> 00:26:51.480
"Oh, she's the most beautiful woman
in the world."

00:26:51.480 --> 00:26:55.000
"He's the most handsome guy in the world."

00:26:55.000 --> 00:26:59.160
First of all...

00:26:59.160 --> 00:27:03.600
my older brother said something really funny, he
said to me, "Do you like that girl?" I answered, "Yes."

00:27:03.600 --> 00:27:06.080
He said, "Do you want to spend your life with her?" I
said, "Yes."

00:27:06.080 --> 00:27:11.160
He said, "First go to her mother."  "Look at how
her mother looks."

00:27:11.160 --> 00:27:17.080
So I go over and the mother looks terrible. She's overweight, she
looks tired, she looks awful.

00:27:17.080 --> 00:27:24.800
And she said to me, "Well, how do you think she looked
at the beginning?"  So think about it.

00:27:25.480 --> 00:27:30.280
If you're attached to
a person's appearance,

00:27:30.280 --> 00:27:35.240
or something physical, or something not very important
about a person,

00:27:35.240 --> 00:27:38.840
that's going to change, and you're going to see them get
sick, you're going to see them

00:27:38.840 --> 00:27:44.320
age, you're going to see them get diarrhea
and vomit.

00:27:44.320 --> 00:27:49.160
If you're unlucky, you're going to see their insides in surgery
at some point.

00:27:49.160 --> 00:27:53.160
So don't fool yourself into thinking it's

00:27:53.160 --> 00:27:55.840
worth hurting other people

00:27:55.840 --> 00:28:02.000
to get the most beautiful woman or man
you can. It's not worth it. It wo

00:28:02.000 --> 00:28:05.920
n't last.

00:28:05.920 --> 00:28:09.320
It's great to have a relationship, but have it
for the right reason.

00:28:09.320 --> 00:28:12.080
Okay, next.

00:28:13.000 --> 00:28:16.160
If you have an anger problem

00:28:16.160 --> 00:28:18.400
or get annoyed easily,

00:28:18.400 --> 00:28:21.880
then fantasize about giving this person

00:28:21.880 --> 00:28:28.560
something they'll love having.
This is called maitri, jampa, love.

00:28:28.560 --> 00:28:32.240
Fantasize, try to remember
how nice it is to

00:28:32.240 --> 00:28:36.480
give someone something they love,
something they want,

00:28:36.480 --> 00:28:39.840
and try to have this attitude.

00:28:39.840 --> 00:28:43.040
If you don't feel friendly toward another person,

00:28:43.040 --> 00:28:47.000
then have fantasies—which means
meditation—

00:28:47.000 --> 00:28:51.760
about giving them something
they really like.

00:28:51.760 --> 00:28:54.080
The next one.

00:28:54.080 --> 00:28:55.840
It's... I'm

00:28:55.840 --> 00:29:01.480
going to give you a moment to  This one. I bet you ca
n't remember what this one is.

00:29:01.480 --> 00:29:06.680
Tim's cheating by looking ahead.

00:29:08.040 --> 00:29:11.000
What was this one again?

00:29:11.000 --> 00:29:14.920
Okay, this one's about pride.

00:29:14.920 --> 00:29:18.800
Pride is also going to be a hindrance
to keeping your vows.

00:29:18.800 --> 00:29:23.000
And one of the most common kinds of pride

00:29:23.000 --> 00:29:29.000
in a monastic setting, which is where
this book was taught,

00:29:29.000 --> 00:29:37.040
is: How much do you know about the scriptures?
How many events have you accumulated in your life?

00:29:37.040 --> 00:29:42.000
And this is something I really enjoy, the unknown events of the Dharma,

00:29:42.000 --> 00:29:46.840
and the more you accumulate, the more you feel
like you're special.

00:29:46.840 --> 00:29:49.680
And Pabongka Rinpoche said,

00:29:49.680 --> 00:29:53.000
"All the Dharma you have learned in your life,
all the things you have memorized,

00:29:53.000 --> 00:29:58.480
all the things you have debated,
all the degrees of Geshe you could have,

00:29:58.480 --> 00:30:03.160
compared to what you have left to learn, you
know nothing."

00:30:03.160 --> 00:30:08.920
You're like a worm at the bottom of the sea."

00:30:08.920 --> 00:30:13.320
And sometimes you come up and see the stars.

00:30:13.320 --> 00:30:16.640
Many of those stars have planets around them.


00:30:16.640 --> 00:30:22.800
There are people on those planets. There are things
to know about those people.

00:30:22.800 --> 00:30:27.680
The things we know that we're
so proud to know

00:30:27.680 --> 00:30:35.400
are a very, very, very small fraction
of what you could know.

00:30:35.400 --> 00:30:37.200
So don't be proud.

00:30:37.200 --> 00:30:39.840
Next.

00:30:43.000 --> 00:30:47.800
One of the biggest motivations
for breaking your vows

00:30:47.800 --> 00:30:52.120
or your commitments, your morality, which will prevent you from
reaching nirvana,

00:30:52.120 --> 00:30:58.640
which will prevent you from reaching the second level
of Lam Rim, personal nirvana,

00:30:58.640 --> 00:31:02.080
is understanding emptiness, studying emptiness.

00:31:02.080 --> 00:31:07.040
If you realize that the bad things

00:31:07.040 --> 00:31:09.680
someone is doing to you

00:31:09.680 --> 00:31:13.960
are coming directly from what you did
last week,

00:31:13.960 --> 00:31:19.120
then you're not going to make big mistakes.
The more you can study emptiness,

00:31:19.120 --> 00:31:23.280
the more you can study cause and effect,
dependent origination,

00:31:23.280 --> 00:31:26.240
which means, "That person comes
from my seeds,"

00:31:26.240 --> 00:31:32.160
then it's going to be easier to keep
your vows. It's going to be easier.

00:31:32.160 --> 00:31:35.600
So study, study, study. I

00:31:35.600 --> 00:31:38.920
had a teacher,  He said...

00:31:38.920 --> 00:31:42.560
an old Mongolian master,

00:31:42.560 --> 00:31:46.800
very old, with tuberculosis.

00:31:46.800 --> 00:31:49.440
He used to say:

00:31:49.440 --> 00:31:57.120
"He is very good.  You're so proud, you have
a lot of Princeton pride,

00:31:57.120 --> 00:32:01.760
"and then the Geshe thing, that's very useful,
very useful.

00:32:01.760 --> 00:32:06.560
" So you'll push yourself harder
just to look smart.

00:32:06.560 --> 00:32:11.960
"That's fortunate, but later on,
try to give that up.

00:32:11.960 --> 00:32:14.040
Just study to be a good person."

00:32:14.040 --> 00:32:16.440
It's very funny.  He gave me

00:32:16.440 --> 00:32:20.000
Adam's text
on his deathbed.

00:32:20.000 --> 00:32:23.080
I remember this.

00:32:24.040 --> 00:32:26.720
The following

00:32:27.560 --> 00:32:31.920
is technically the fourth cause, is it
?  No, whatever.

00:32:31.920 --> 00:32:36.000
One of the reasons for breaking your vows
or losing your commitments

00:32:36.000 --> 00:32:40.200
is that it is very difficult in the modern world

00:32:40.200 --> 00:32:44.560
to keep your mind on your vows when you are
very busy.

00:32:44.560 --> 00:32:46.800
When things are moving
very fast

00:32:46.800 --> 00:32:49.720
and there are a thousand things to see on the internet,

00:32:49.720 --> 00:32:53.120
and life is moving very fast,

00:32:53.120 --> 00:32:58.320
it's difficult to maintain that self-awareness

00:32:58.320 --> 00:33:04.200
of: "Am I breaking my vows, am I doing
something to hurt someone?"

00:33:04.200 --> 00:33:09.000
So you need to slow down,
return to your vows,

00:33:09.000 --> 00:33:15.000
and maintain some kind of sensitivity, some
awareness,

00:33:15.000 --> 00:33:20.000
to the fact that you have commitments
not to hurt people.

00:33:20.000 --> 00:33:25.040
The busier things get,
the more careful you have to be.

00:33:25.040 --> 00:33:27.360
It's easy to have... It

00:33:27.360 --> 00:33:31.480
's even easy to get annoyed with your partner
when you're very busy.  They're

00:33:31.480 --> 00:33:34.000
trying to tell you something

00:33:34.000 --> 00:33:37.880
and you have ten things happening
at work,

00:33:37.880 --> 00:33:42.880
and you're like, "Look, I don't have time
to listen to you right now.

00:33:42.880 --> 00:33:46.480
My boss gave me ten things to do."

00:33:46.480 --> 00:33:49.280
Those are the moments when you need to slow down


00:33:49.280 --> 00:33:51.320
and return to your vows,

00:33:51.320 --> 00:33:54.240
and don't forget your commitment to be kind
to people,

00:33:54.240 --> 00:33:59.240
even when you're very stressed,
very busy.

00:33:59.960 --> 00:34:03.880
It's better to break some

00:34:03.880 --> 00:34:09.400
business commitments than to get nervous, stressed, and unfriendly to people.

00:34:09.400 --> 00:34:15.040
It's better not to pay a bill or miss a business meeting

00:34:15.040 --> 00:34:19.400
or not do your best
at your job,

00:34:19.400 --> 00:34:23.480
if that means keeping
your mind clear.

00:34:25.080 --> 00:34:27.600
Next image.

00:34:27.600 --> 00:34:32.600
This is a lady buying something useless
in the store.

00:34:33.400 --> 00:34:36.920
See if you can remember this story.

00:34:36.920 --> 00:34:40.840
She said, "Oh, this box is very beautiful."  She
went to a department store.

00:34:40.840 --> 00:34:47.680
She bought this... What's it like?  What is that place
for the house, where you buy things?

00:34:47.680 --> 00:34:49.320
Crate and Barrel.

00:34:49.320 --> 00:34:51.800
She went to Crate and Barrel in the United States and
bought this.

00:34:51.800 --> 00:34:54.640
She said, "Oh, my husband is going to love this box
."

00:34:54.640 --> 00:34:58.160
She has no idea what she's going to use it for,

00:34:58.160 --> 00:35:01.960
but she's going to take it home.

00:35:04.320 --> 00:35:05.080
Then,

00:35:05.080 --> 00:35:09.920
when she gets home, her husband will say, "Are you crazy?
This is just a little box that's useless.

00:35:09.920 --> 00:35:13.320
We have enough junk in the house."  "

00:35:13.320 --> 00:35:15.880
Give it back, get your money back."

00:35:15.880 --> 00:35:22.600
Now, should I go to the gas station
and try to return it?

00:35:24.120 --> 00:35:30.960
No, that's not where she got the box.
It's obvious, but we have to mention it.

00:35:31.480 --> 00:35:34.240
If you buy a stupid box

00:35:34.240 --> 00:35:39.080
because you liked it and think your husband will
like it, which he won't,

00:35:39.080 --> 00:35:42.800
and he convinces you to return it,

00:35:42.800 --> 00:35:46.720
don't return it to a different place,
return it to the place where you bought it.

00:35:46.720 --> 00:35:49.840
What does that mean?

00:35:56.040 --> 00:35:58.800
You should pay me.

00:35:59.680 --> 00:36:03.560
When it's time to confess,
when you've broken a vow,

00:36:03.560 --> 00:36:07.680
then try to go back to the person
who gave you the vow.

00:36:07.680 --> 00:36:12.160
Try to confess in front of the person
who gave you the vow. Is

00:36:12.160 --> 00:36:17.080
it okay to confess at home alone?

00:36:17.680 --> 00:36:21.520
Not for vows you took from other people.

00:36:21.520 --> 00:36:24.040
Generally,

00:36:24.040 --> 00:36:27.320
if you didn't take a vow from someone else,

00:36:27.320 --> 00:36:29.320
then maybe it's okay to do it at home,

00:36:29.320 --> 00:36:34.480
confess in front of a Buddha statue or something,
in extreme cases it's okay.

00:36:34.480 --> 00:36:36.560
But generally,

00:36:36.560 --> 00:36:40.160
if you can go back to the person
who gave you your vows

00:36:40.160 --> 00:36:45.960
and confess to them  Openly, without shame.
We're shameless all day long.

00:36:45.960 --> 00:36:50.040
So, to be shameless about your vows,
just say, "What the hell."

00:36:50.040 --> 00:36:53.280
Go straight to your teacher and say,
"I tore up this stupid vow."

00:36:53.280 --> 00:36:57.560
And your teacher is like, "Wow!"  "You're a
very bad person!" And you say, "Yes, I am." Get over

00:36:57.560 --> 00:37:03.120
it. And then you feel so clean,
you feel so good. You

00:37:04.120 --> 00:37:07.960
can be shy about a lot of things
in your life, but don't be shy about your vows.

00:37:07.960 --> 00:37:11.240
If you break a vow, tell someone,

00:37:11.240 --> 00:37:14.560
and that's how you get rid of it.
You get rid of the problem.

00:37:14.560 --> 00:37:18.600
If you keep it and hide it, if you spend more time hiding it

00:37:18.600 --> 00:37:23.720
than confessing it, or holding onto it,
then it's just foolish,

00:37:23.720 --> 00:37:27.560
and you won't feel good, you won't feel clean.

00:37:27.560 --> 00:37:33.200
Just be upfront with your teachers:
"I have this problem."  "I have this bad habit."

00:37:33.640 --> 00:37:37.800
The karma is destroyed, the seed is destroyed.

00:37:38.480 --> 00:37:42.600
And you know, your teacher is going to say, "I've heard
that before, you've told me that before."

00:37:42.600 --> 00:37:46.920
But be persistent and keep telling them.

00:37:48.440 --> 00:37:51.120
Next picture.

